@@ -2797,3 +2797,52 @@ count. Without observed rounds they are `null`, with `unavailable_reason`, rathe
 than being inferred from output tokens. Acceptance is accepted draft tokens divided
 by proposed draft tokens; the bonus token is excluded. Native MTP, ngram and DFlash
 counters keep their existing meanings.
+
+### Completed-step historical GC extension
+
+The opt-in `--kvmem-gc-statistical` policy accepts a development `kvmem_gc` field on
+text-only `/v1/chat/completions` requests with an explicit `prompt_cache_key`.
+It requires one request lane and a RAM-only KVMem history repository; media and
+grafted prefixes are rejected. The flag is exclusive with LRU/redundancy GC.
+Without application evidence it does not infer completed thinking or delete it.
+
+The field contains `prefix_tokens`, `prefix_sha256`, and `steps` (1..64 entries).
+The digest is lowercase SHA256 of the actual prepared input token IDs, each
+encoded as little-endian uint32, rather than a hash of the visible text.
+For evidence preparation, `POST /apply-template` accepts `return_tokens: true`
+and additionally returns `tokens`, an array of `{id, piece}` rows from the actual
+prepared prompt. A piece is text or a byte array for an incomplete UTF-8 fragment.
+Use these IDs rather than re-tokenizing the flattened rendered text: literal
+special-token spellings in message content do not have template-token identity.
+Omitting this flag preserves the existing prompt-only response.
+Each step supplies `id`, `kind`, `source_begin`, `source_end`, `result_begin`,
+`result_end`, `observation_id`, `importance`, `cold`, and `complete`. Ranges are
+half-open token coordinates in that prepared input. Supported kinds are
+`thinking`, `completed_step`, `tool_detail`, and `superseded`; a kind is not
+proof of redundancy. Source and retained-result ranges must be disjoint and
+contain full 64-token blocks. Mixed boundaries, sink, recent and active readers
+retain their normal protections.
+
+The default thresholds are `--kvmem-gc-min-observations 3`,
+`--kvmem-gc-min-cold-observations 3`, and `--kvmem-gc-max-importance 0.1`.
+The application must provide real observations with increasing IDs; repeating
+an identical observation is idempotent, not another cold sample. Completed
+steps meeting the thresholds can retire below the pressure watermark. Candidate
+selection checks published eligibility before later reselection; physical Host
+release may follow after current owners finish. There is no strict real-time
+guarantee that every pair of decode calls contains a completed GC worker round.
+
+Malformed or mismatched evidence returns HTTP 400. Publication is transactional.
+The directory tracks at most 64 live steps. Source retirement releases completed
+step metadata and its additional result protection. A full directory evicts old
+advisory evidence, retaining its KV and invalidating old deletion proposals; it
+does not delete unproven content to admit a new step. A genuine prefix rewind
+invalidates affected evidence and bindings.
+
+`GET /props?model=MODEL` exposes `kvmem_gc.policy`, `min_observations`,
+`min_cold_observations`, `max_importance`, `block_tokens`, and `ram_only` from
+that model's actual options. A verified-artifact producer must check these
+values before using the distinct one-file-equality profile (1 observation,
+0 cold observations, maximum importance 1). That profile does not manufacture
+attention statistics or authorize arbitrary thinking removal. Native CLI/chat
+schema, full CUDA execution and model-quality acceptance are separate checks.
